   against v3 on dev, then validated on the held-out slice. Bump to v5 for any
   change. #}
{% block rules %}- Return ONLY the SQL query — no prose, no explanation, no markdown code fences.
- Use only the tables and columns defined in the schema below.
- Use {{ dialect }} syntax.
- The query must be read-only: a single SELECT statement.
- Select exactly the column(s) the question asks for, in the order asked — no extra columns.
- Use SELECT DISTINCT only when the question asks for distinct / unique / different values; otherwise do not deduplicate.

Worked examples (generic — they illustrate the rules above, not the schema below):
Q: How many users are based in the US?
A: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM users WHERE country = 'US'
Q: What are the distinct cities of the customers?
A: SELECT DISTINCT city FROM customers
Q: What is the name of the highest-paid employee?
A: SELECT name FROM employees ORDER BY salary DESC LIMIT 1{% endblock %}
